      <section class="process-section" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The process shelf</p>
          <h2 id="process-title">Heatwork over time, from slip to table.</h2>
          <p>From first pinch pot to dinnerware you use every week. Small classes, real firing, finished pieces you can pick up after the kiln cools.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-shell">
          <div class="process-photo">
            <img src="assets/potter-hands-centering-wet-clay-wheel.jpg" alt="Hands centering wet clay on a pottery wheel" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <svg class="ring-lines" viewBox="0 0 220 220" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="88"></circle>
              <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="58"></circle>
              <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="28"></circle>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="process-track" aria-label="Ceramic process steps">
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>01</span>
              <h3>Center clay</h3>
              <p>We wedge, weigh, and center a forgiving stoneware body before the first pull.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>02</span>
              <h3>Pull walls</h3>
              <p>Hands learn pressure, water, speed, and the quiet timing of the wheel.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>03</span>
              <h3>Trim foot rings</h3>
              <p>Leather-hard work returns for trimming, signatures, and a foot that sits cleanly.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>04</span>
              <h3>Bisque fire</h3>
              <p>Pieces dry slowly, then bisque so they can handle glaze without cracking.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>05</span>
              <h3>Brush glaze</h3>
              <p>Glaze tests, not guesswork: brush, dip, trail, and record what each surface needs.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>06</span>
              <h3>Cone 6 firing</h3>
              <p>Electric cone-fired surfaces finish under measured heatwork and kiln notes.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="process-card">
              <span>07</span>
              <h3>Pickup / table use</h3>
              <p>Most workshop pieces are ready two to four weeks later, boxed for pickup.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="workshops-section" id="workshops" aria-labelledby="workshops-title">
        <div class="section-heading split-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Workshops & memberships</p>
            <h2 id="workshops-title">For first-timers and people with clay under their nails.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Beginner-friendly options, small class sizes, materials and firing included. Returning makers can reserve open studio time, glaze lab hours, and shelf space.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="offering-grid">
          <article class="offering-card">
            <img src="assets/potter-hands-centering-wet-clay-wheel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">Beginner - 2 hours</p>
              <h3>First-Time Wheel Night</h3>
              <p>Center, open, and pull a small cup or bowl with close coaching.</p>
              <span>Clay, trimming, glazing, and firing included.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="offering-card">
            <img src="assets/ceramic-artist-brushing-glaze-handmade-vessel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">All levels - 2.5 hours</p>
              <h3>Handbuilding Table</h3>
              <p>Pinch, coil, slab, and texture trays, vases, planters, and sculptural objects.</p>
              <span>Best for groups who want room to talk.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="offering-card feature-offer">
            <img src="assets/shelves-wheel-thrown-mugs-bowls-vases-studio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">Returning - 6 weeks</p>
              <h3>Six-Week Throwing Series</h3>
              <p>Build repeatable cylinders, bowls, handles, lids, trimming habits, and glaze records across a full firing cycle.</p>
              <span>For people ready to practice with continuity.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="offering-card">
            <img src="assets/close-up-ceramic-glaze-test-tiles-studio-wall.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">Curious makers - 90 min</p>
              <h3>Glaze Lab</h3>
              <p>Read test tiles, choose surfaces, and learn why thickness, clay body, and heat matter.</p>
              <span>Bring bisque or use studio forms.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="offering-card">
            <img src="assets/ceramic-kiln-interior-glowing-orange-heat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">Private - 2 hours</p>
              <h3>Group / Date Night</h3>
              <p>A hosted table or wheel session for birthdays, teams, couples, and visiting family.</p>
              <span>Pickup timeline confirmed before you leave.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="offering-card">
            <img src="assets/shelves-wheel-thrown-mugs-bowls-vases-studio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div>
              <p class="tag">Members - monthly</p>
              <h3>Member Open Studio</h3>
              <p>Reserved wheels, shared tools, clay purchase, bisque shelves, and glaze firing access.</p>
              <span>For makers who can work independently.</span>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
